\DOC LOCAL_MONTMUL_P256_TAC

\TYPE {LOCAL_MONTMUL_P256_TAC : int -> string list -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Advances a machine-state symbolic-execution goal across one inlined
Montgomery-multiplication subroutine, replacing the current state variable by
its successor and adding an assumption characterising the product written to
the destination buffer.

\DESCRIBE
The first argument is an {int}, the offset/index locating the call site in the
program being stepped; the second is a {string list} naming the destination and
the two source operands of the multiplication, these names selecting which
stored values the new assumption relates. The goal it is applied to has an
{eventually} conclusion whose assumptions describe the contents of registers
and memory blocks in the current state {s}, together with a program-counter
assumption, a {bytes_loaded} assumption and a {MAYCHANGE} frame relating the
initial state to {s}. A fresh successor state {s'} is introduced, and every
assumption mentioning {s} is discharged and re-added with {s'} in its place:
the program-counter assumption now records the address after the subroutine,
and the {MAYCHANGE} frame now relates the initial state to {s'} and may gain a
component for the destination buffer. Two assumptions are new: one stating that
the destination buffer in {s'} holds the named result value, and one giving the
conditional Montgomery-product specification of that value in terms of the two
named operands. Purely arithmetic and non-overlapping assumptions are retained
unchanged, though reordered.
{
             A ?- eventually ... s
    ===================================== LOCAL_MONTMUL_P256_TAC i ["dest"; "src1"; "src2"]
             A' ?- eventually ... s'
}
\noindent where {A'} consists of the re-stated assumptions about {s'} plus the
two new assumptions, as described above.

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this single-subgoal state-advancing behaviour,
always on goals of the same form: an {eventually} conclusion with a full set of
machine-state assumptions for the current state.

\ENDDOC
